 two in our  local markets learn the lay of the land  with respect to all of these different  problems that we're having today and  then likely partner with the Obama  foundation is kind of a big umbrella and  then you know we're planning to be in  this fight for for the long haul we're  interested in making a difference we're  interested in educating people on racial  injustice and because these things have  been going going for decades stacked on  centuries and it's just it just got to a  point where you know if there as I said  there was a mobilization of the group  and I've never seen the group so  determined so we're excited to get  started we know it's a a very long  battle but we've got the stomach for it  and you know we're into it Wow so you  all 30 head coaches in the National  Basketball Association just got together  on a zoom and just started hashing it  out is that what you're saying you're  all got together there was a there was a  white Pierce the as I mentioned coach  Atlanta quail hogs right you know you  know asked for the floor and he had just  a very strong speech to the group about  his sentiments you know he's an Africa  African American coach who grew up  living and seeing all these and justices  and you know it's been going on for  decades and centuries as I mentioned and  George Floyd just it just put everybody  over the top which which is saying a lot  and so personally I'm partnering with a  group in Dallas called  mothers against police brutality which  is a  phenomenal group of people that are a  grassroots organization in Dallas only  and we've got a meeting scheduled with  the mayor of Dallas tomorrow afternoon  and you know we plan to to start start  the conversation and and and and partner  with as many people as we can that  didn't have real influence in all of our  cities to to try to effect change and  you were the head coach when Steven  Jackson was with the Pacers Rick so and  you know clearly obviously um that  George Floyd was a close personal friend  of Stephens who and he has been just  remarkable and personalizing and and  being there for the family as well as  bringing home to anyone who may need to  know about George Floyd that here was a  real man a real person who had an  officer put put his knee on on his neck  and kill him in the streets of  Minneapolis I mean he was it Stephens  been remarkable for that image frozen in  time will be one that lives on in  perpetuity it's got to be a major  reminder that you know this this these  things have got to stop Steven Jackson  is not only was a tremendous basketball  player but he's a passionate guy very  animated person and a guy with a great  heart I was with him for multiple years  and he he had a couple of really great  years with Indiana as a player and you  know this has been it's been tragic to  see this happen and I'd have to see his  reaction to it although he's handled it  with with an amazing amount of of grace  and fortitude  Rick Carlisle Dallas Mavericks head  coach here on the Rich Eisen show and  then oh yeah there's a pandemic so  what's going on with with that how are  you preparing with now a schedule and a  location and a date certain by which the  league plans to open are you are you are  you ready to roll  right now Rick how about that is this  question well there's no we're  collecting information I think every  team has one person or another that's on  some kind of committee relative to this  things are becoming clearer and clearer  you know there's been a you know there's  been an understandable hesitation to  throw hard dates out there you know  early on in this process because there's  so many unknowns but you know generally  you know players will be back in market  you know by the 21st of June you know  test testing will start in local local  markets you know there will be a  training camp in your local market for  some period of time and then there will  be a staggered you know movement of  teams to tour land on us that's the  basics that that I know about that I  know that there is an asterisk really  next next to everything in terms of the  level of fluidity that we're dealing  with here so when we're excited to get  back playing you know I know I know our  players are excited I think every  facility has been open now for a while  for individual workouts you know there's  a great amount of care and detail in  keeping the facilities clean you know in  between workouts you know after people  leave at the end of the day etc and you  know we're just we're all gonna have to  have a laser a laser-like focus you know  on everything that we're doing and then  outside like let's let's all hope we get  past the point where the kovat 19 is at  the forefront and that the protocols and  the health and safety measures can allow  everybody to just focus on the  competition you being the seven seed  going in what's your thoughts on the  fact that the schedule in the West you  got eight games that you're gonna have  to play and it may not be very balanced  schedule compared to people that have  this  same number as wins as you right now and  and compared to the East that it's a  simple one because there's just nine  teams and they everyone will play each  other once what do you think of that  well yeah my feeling is that they had to  come up with something that made sense  and what makes sense isn't necessarily  going to have great symmetry in this  situation you know I my understanding is  that we will likely be playing our next  eight games on the schedule which does  make sense and most of those games were  were against teams that are going to be  playing so in in the in Orlando so  mmm-hmm hey we got to keep our eye on  the ball we got a you know take care of  our own business I'd not get too much  into analysis of other people's  situations try to do everything possible  to get our players in the best possible  condition in the right way we've never  had a situation where we come off of a  three month layoff quite like this  normally when you come off the summer  you know players will report around  voluntarily report around Labor Day and  then you'll have a three week period it  kind of fades everybody in you know with  voluntary workouts pickup games and so  forth along with work with your strength  coaches this hasn't this hasn't been  that level of normalcy and so we're  dealing with a different you know a far  different set of circumstances but we  have a lot of smart people in this  league we have a lot of smart people on  all these teams and you know we'll work  through it meticulously and in terms of  your personal team and issues that might  be you know obviously I think  everybody's got players who might be in  Europe I mean to your best our sheltered  in place there how much contact do you  have with with Luca throughout this  entire process in porzingis coach yeah  we got contact with them they've been on  zoom' calls you know you know that all  that will be will be taken care of in  terms of them being back here at the  right time and  and we'll proceed from there but it's in  you know this just three month period  and it really it's amazing to me that  it's gone by as quickly as it has I mean  the first week or two seemed to drag and  then I somehow or other it's all gone by  pretty fast and you know in another two  weeks you know we'll be in the midst of  testing and then getting ready for for  you know our local training camp  situations to begin so we're excited but  but cautiousness as well and there will  continue to be a lot of communication  throughout our league you know on best  practices as we get back into you know  these workouts with our players etc and  you know safety is is the number-one  concern  straight across the board a couple more  questions for you Rick Carlisle Dallas  Mavericks head coach any conversation  being had with the coaches in your zoom  or with the players in terms of any  protest that is going to be expected to  be had prior to any games during any  workouts prior to any games based on  what is going on in the real world I  know there's been a conversation about  what the NFL may do but the NBA is gonna  be first up if we're knocking on wood  everything goes according to plan kovat  wise any conversation on that front of  what you're hearing Rick all right now  that the coaches are focused on you know  as I mentioned an action plan involving  all 30 markets to to really dive into  something that's going to be individual  in nature because everybody's mark it's  going to be a little different but we're  all going to be under the same umbrella  and we're gonna all have to a great  degree similar messaging and so you know  when you're talking about progress you  know a peaceful protest can be part of  that but but so far our conversations  have really been about you know how  we're going to be able to proceed and  progress you know when when there were  situations involving possible protests  in the last several years what I can  tell you is that you  with our organization with the Mavericks  Mark Cuban and myself in talking to our  players said hey listen guys you know  this is a free country you guys are free  to do whatever you wish you're free to  express yourselves however you wish and  but we we urge you to talk about what  you're going to do and and and let us  know if you're going to do something  just so we're aware and we never had any  any protesting things happen with our  team and you know there were some teams  that that still do they still lock arms  during the net the national anthem as a  show of togetherness and things like  that  you know I I don't know what's going to  what if anything is going to happen but  you know we love the fact that the  conversation conversation has opened up  and it's going it's going to be animated  and but we believe it's going to be  ongoing last one for you Rick I would be  remiss if I did not point out t